session:pr133Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Adds a new rdf_canon workspace crate that wraps the rdf-canon library (v0.15, RDFC-1.0 / URDNA2015) to provide deterministic canonicalization of Dagalog Datastore datasets. Implements Option A from docs/plans/CANON_PLAN.md — using the existing rdf-canon crate rather than a hand-rolled implementation, so all three canonicalization phases (#69, #70, #71) are delivered in a single PR. Public API ``rust /// Canonicalize the full dataset to N-Quads (RDFC-1.0). pub fn canonicalize_dataset(store: &Datastore) -> Result<String, String> /// Canonicalize a single named graph (or default graph when graph_id == 0). pub fn canonicalize_graph(store: &Datastore, graph_id: GraphElementId) -> Result<String, String> ` canonicalize_graph is what the records backend needs for per-content-graph checksumming (IRecordBackend.ToCanonString()). Details Converts Datastore quads → oxrdf::Dataset → rdf-canon → sorted N-Quads string Blank nodes get canonical labels _:c14n0, _:c14n1, … Isomorphic datasets (same structure, different blank node names) produce identical output rdf-canon uses oxrdf 0.2 (the existing turtle crate uses 0.3`) — they coexist without conflict" ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:133 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr133 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
